  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Issue:\n\nRight now the \"World Preload Completed\" Notification doesn't do much. It only tells you that it's done but you can't actually join the Instance with it.  \n\nThe fact that \"Accept\" also basically just removes the notification was quite confusing to me, as I expected it to make me join the instance, just like pressing on accept on an Invite does.\n\n# Suggestion:\n\nMake the \"World Preload Completed\" Notification more useful by doing the following:  \n\n- pressing on the checkmark should make you Join the Instance (Just link Invites do) \n\n- add a separate decline button  \n\n- move it over to the Invites section (cause with the changes from above it basically just becomes an Invite)\n\n \n\n# Additional Info:\n\nI would like for the World Preloade and Join Instance after having waited in a Queue to be relatively similar. It's quite hard to setup a test for Group Queues, so I couldn't really compare them.",
